# Admin auth — agent reference

Applies whenever a change touches the `/bookings` routes, the new admin-only edge functions, or guest-form non-production API toggles.

## 1. Auth model

- Provider: **Supabase Auth** with **Google OAuth**.
- Client: `@supabase/supabase-js` (add to `ui/package.json` when implementing).
- Single shared Supabase client: `ui/src/lib/supabase/client.ts`.
- Entry point: **`/for-hosts/login`** — calls `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'google' })`. Legacy **`/sign-in`** redirects here.

## 2. Allow list (server)

- **`ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS`** (edge only) — comma-separated emails for `verifyAdminJwt` and `isPlatformAdmin`. Org **owners** can pass `verifyAdminJwt` without being on this list.
- **`SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS`** (edge only) — platform `/admin/*` APIs (`serveSuperAdmin`, `list-developments`, …).
- **`VITE_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS`** (UI / Vercel) — client UX gate for the Admin mode tab and `RequireSuperAdmin`; **not** the security boundary.
- There is **no** `VITE_ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS` — host dashboard access is Google sign-in + org/team RBAC; do not reintroduce a client allow list.

## 3. Route guards (UI)

- `RequireAdmin.tsx` — loader while session hydrates; redirects to **`/for-hosts/login`** if unsigned. **No client email allow list.**
- `RequireSuperAdmin.tsx` — checks `VITE_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS` (UX only); server enforces `SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS`.
- Applied to org/property dashboard routes via `RequireAdmin`; `/admin/*` via `RequireSuperAdmin`.

## 4. Guest form dev controls (`GuestForm.tsx`)

- **Production (`VITE_NODE_ENV === 'production'`):** no dev checkbox panel; submits use full save + storage + calendar + sheet flags as wired in `submit-form`, and **New Booking Request** email runs by default (`sendEmail` omitted → treated as on server-side).
- **Non-production:** dev panel shows save/storage/calendar/sheet/**Send email** toggles (**all on by default**; uncheck to skip). Flags are sent as **FormData** fields (not URL query params). **`sendEmail=false`** skips the owner notify only.
- **`?dev=true` is removed** — never gate or preserve this (or `testing` / submit-form control flags) on guest or calendar URLs. Legacy links that still include them are stripped on load.

There is **no** separate test-booking mode, `?testing=true`, `is_test_booking` column, or test-data cleanup edge function — use local/staging projects instead.

## 5. Workflow side effects (admin detail page)

Confirm modals on `/bookings/:bookingId` (Proceed, Back, Cancel) run the orchestrator default happy path for **non-email** effects (DB, PDFs, stay guide). **Outbound emails** are gated by **Property Settings → Email automations** (`propertyAutomationToggles.ts` / `PropertyEmailAutomationsSection`).

**Optional email checkboxes** appear on **forward** Proceed confirms when either:

1. **Past stay dates** — `status` is `PENDING_REVIEW`, `PENDING_DOCUMENTS`, or `READY_FOR_CHECKIN` and check-in or check-out is strictly before today (Asia/Manila); or
2. **Re-forward after regression** — the booking still has artifacts from a later pipeline step (request/approved PDFs, doc completions, stay guide, SD form email, etc.) after admin **Return to …**, guest-field revert, or similar.

In those cases, each email that would fire on that transition is shown as a checkbox **default unchecked**. Checked boxes send `devControls` on `transition-booking` (`sendGafRequestEmail`, `sendBookingAcknowledgementEmail`, `sendPetRequestEmail`, `sendParkingBroadcastEmail`, `sendReadyForCheckinEmail`, `sendSdRefundFormEmail`). Normal forward proceeds (no past dates, no regression) omit `devControls` — all applicable emails still follow property automations.

Server-side `DevControlFlags` in `_shared/workflowOrchestrator.ts` are also used by automated callers (approval webhook, cron, import revert).

| Email / effect                                                                 | Production control                                              |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| New booking request (guest submit)                                             | Guest form dev **Send email** (non-prod only; §4)               |
| GAF / pet request PDFs + emails                                                | Property automation toggles + resolved `documentRequirements[]` |
| Booking acknowledgement, parking broadcast, ready-for-check-in, SD refund form | Property automation toggles                                     |
| Manual re-send SD refund form                                                  | **Automation Triggers** on booking detail                       |

## 6. Server contract

- All admin edge functions (`list-bookings`, `transition-booking`, `upload-booking-asset`, `send-sd-refund-form-email`, `parking-broadcast-email`, `cancel-booking`, …) set **`verify_jwt = false`** in `supabase/config.toml` **and** must call `verifyAdminJwt(req)` as the first line of the handler.
  - **Why `false` in config.toml:** Kong's `verify_jwt = true` gate uses the legacy HS256 JWT secret and rejects newer ES256 auth tokens issued by Supabase local dev (≥ 1.x). Our `verifyAdminJwt` calls `supabase.auth.getUser(jwt)` which handles both algorithms correctly **and** also enforces the `ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS` allow-list — making it a strictly stronger gate than Kong's check.
  - **The function body check IS the security boundary** — never skip `verifyAdminJwt(req)` on the assumption that Kong already validated the token.
- The public functions (`submit-form`, `get-form`, `get-booked-dates`, `get-guest-payment-info`, `get-sd-form`, `submit-sd-form`) keep `verify_jwt = false` — guests must still be able to hit them with only the anon key.
- **`copy-property-settings`** is **not** a `verifyAdminJwt` admin function. It uses `serveAuthenticated` + **`verifyPropertyAccess`**: source requires `settings:view`; each selected group on each target is checked for that group's edit leaf(s) (and plan feature when gated). Permission/plan misses are **skipped and reported** per target/group — the batch does not hard-fail. Same-org targets only. See `.cursor/rules/supabase-edge-functions.mdc` and `docs/guides/routes/org/properties.md`.

