## 8. Step-up OTP for sensitive super-admin actions

Every **mutating** branch of a gated `serveSuperAdmin` function calls
`requireSuperAdminStepUp(req, user, '<action>')` (`_shared/superAdminVerification.ts`) as
its first line. GET/HEAD/OPTIONS always pass; a missing/expired sudo token returns
`401 { code: 'SUPERADMIN_OTP_REQUIRED', action }` and the mutation does not run.

- **Flow:** `super-admin-verification` edge fn — `send_otp` mails a 6-digit code (hashed,
  10-min TTL, rate-limited 3 / 15 min) to the **acting super admin's own login email**;
  `verify_otp` returns an HMAC sudo token (15-min TTL, bound to `user.id`).
- **Client:** `edgeClient.ts` stores the token in `sessionStorage`, sends it as
  `x-superadmin-otp` on every edge call, and on a `SUPERADMIN_OTP_REQUIRED` 401 opens
  `SuperAdminOtpDialog` (via `SuperAdminStepUpProvider` in `SuperAdminShell`) then retries
  the request once. `x-superadmin-otp` is allow-listed in `_shared/cors.ts`.
- **Challenges table:** `super_admin_verification_challenges` (platform-scoped, no
  org/property FK). Audit: `super_admin.step_up_requested` / `.step_up_verified`.
- **Gated functions:** `org-subscriptions-admin`, `platform-payment-settings`,
  `platform-parking-settings`, `parking-payouts`, `ai-platform-credit-wallet`,
  `ai-platform-global-settings`, `dashboard-assistant-global-settings`, `pricing-plans`,
  `platform-settings`, `update-platform-host-settings`, `decide-contract-consideration`,
  `ai-platform-generation-overrides`.
  Add a row to `GATED_SUPER_ADMIN_ACTIONS` + the guard call to gate a new one.
- Not gated: support tickets, Help Center FAQ CRUD (low risk). The `serveAuthenticated`
  approval-queue functions (`approve-org-verification`, `approve-listing-authorization`, …)
  are a documented follow-up.

Plan / status: [`docs/workflow/in-progress/super-admin-step-up-otp.md`](../docs/workflow/in-progress/super-admin-step-up-otp.md).

## 9. Don'ts

- Don't pass JWTs or admin emails through URL query strings.
- Don't add a second Supabase client — share `ui/src/lib/supabase/client.ts`.
- Don't hardcode `kamehome.azurenorth@gmail.com` in code; read from env.
- Don't build admin features that work without `verifyAdminJwt` server-side — the allow list is the one real gate.

## Host Recommended reward carve-out (R3)

`submit-org-verification` with `tier: 'enhanced'` normally requires plan feature `recommendedBadgeEligible`. When `platform_settings.host_reward_enabled` is true, the campaign window is open, and the org is under `host_reward_max_per_org`, that gate is **skipped** so Free hosts can submit Recommended for the campaign. Keep the gate for everyone else. Grant/expire/revoke live in `_shared/hostVerificationReward.ts` (not a general entitlement bypass).
